{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review Public Transport Equivalent Costs in Disabled Students' Allowance",
        "additional_details": "We call on the Government to reform how the Student Loans Company calculates Public Transport Equivalent Costs (PTEC) for Disabled Students' Allowance. We feel current calculations often ignore real-world situations, forcing disabled students to pay more than their non-disabled peers to access education. We think the rules should be reviewed so PTEC reflects actual travel costs and does not create a financial penalty for disability.",
        "background": "We urge the Government to review the regulations and establish a system that reflects the real costs faced by students today so that disabled students are not financially disadvantaged when accessing education due to inaccurate transport cost calculations.",
